    "label": null,
    "number": "Theorem 2",
    "quote": "Suppose that (2) holds with ∆ satisfying ∆i > 0 for all i ∈ V, where V ( [K] is an arbitrary nonempty set of actions. Suppose that there exists D ≥ 0 such that E[sum_t max_{i∈[K]\\V} E_t[l_i^t − l_{i*}^t]] ≤ D ... The regret for the Tsallis-INF with IW estimators will then be bounded as R^T_{i*} ≤ O(sum_{i∈V} log T/∆i + sqrt(C sum_{i∈V} log T/∆i) + D + K)."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Explicit form in appendix (79): 25 log(T+1) sum 1/Delta_i + 10 sqrt(C log(T+1) sum 1/Delta_i) + 2(K+D). Stochastic case with multiple optimal arms: C = D = 0 and V = {Delta_i > 0}, giving O(sum log T/Delta_i). Corrupted stochastic: D = C. sum_subopt is used for the sum over V."
  },
